"""Grade 10 Hindi — Cambridge IGCSE Hindi as a Second Language (0549) style, year 2 of 2 (exam year).

Eight theme units followed by two exam-skills units (Paper 1 reading and writing, Paper 2 listening).
Reading items use original passages (articles, blogs, adverts, job notices); listening-style items are
written as transcripts of original conversations, interviews, news bulletins and announcements; grammar
(वाच्य, संधि-समास, common errors) and vocabulary are tested in context; writing tasks follow the 0549
forms (ई-मेल, लेख, रिपोर्ट) with level-based Hindi mark schemes. All text is original and in Hindi.

Shared factories come from g8_hindi.py (reading, writing, tagbank, xform, meanings ...) and g9_hindi.py
(शीर्षक मिलाना, नोट्स, सारांश). This file adds the तथ्य/राय and भ्रामक-विकल्प factories and the units.
The exam-skills units (9, 10) re-use this year's passages as practice papers, as a revision unit would.
"""
